// ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
// B11. RIGHT JOIN: the employees that manage nobody stay on the m side.
// Question: Over all employees as managers and the employees that report to
//   them, how many employees are on each side, and what do they earn?
// B9 to B13 run one self-join query with each join type. e is the employee
// and m is the manager, joined on e.mgr = m.empno. KING has no manager, and 8
// employees manage nobody. The join type decides which rows reach each
// measure. No join type makes a measure count a row twice, and NULL-padded
// rows add nothing.
//
// RIGHT gives 21 joined rows. The 8 employees that manage nobody are kept on
// the m side. Their rows are NULL-padded on the e side, so the e measures are
// the same as for INNER (B9).
// Spec: 7.6, 8.1, G2 (8.3), A.6
// ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
// KQL: a RIGHT JOIN, written as a LEFT JOIN with the sides swapped: all employees as managers m, and their reports e.
FIND emp m, m [empno = mgr] + emp e
FETCH agg(e.emp_count) ecount, agg(e.sum_sal) esal, agg(m.emp_count) mcount, agg(m.sum_sal) msal
